        "text": "{\"recorded_count\": 22, \"total_count\": 22, \"missing_ids\": [], \"complete\": true, \"results\": [{\"item_id\": \"FT-1\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Create (Fitness): \\\"Hydrow Wave Rower\\\" saved with name/price/rating/image/link/tags/3 specs/description/review/featured and appeared instantly in /category/fitness, /products and its detail page. Edit (Home): Dyson V15 Detect price 749→729, rating 4.7→4.2, tags rewritten, featured off — all reflected instantly. Edit (→Tech): Hydrow re-saved with every field changed — name→\\\"Hydrow Wave Rower Pro\\\", price→$1,699, rating→4.8, category Fitness→Tech, description→\\\"EDITED brief:…\\\", review→\\\"EDITED REVIEW BODY…\\\", image→photo-1517836357463…?w=900, link→https://example.com/hydrow-wave-pro, tags→+pro-trim, spec Screen→\\\"22-inch HD touchscreen\\\" and spec 3 renamed to \\\"Seat rail / Extended, fits up to 6ft 6in\\\", featured retained. Tech category grid and the detail page both show all new values immediately. (In-session only — persistence failure recorded separately under FT-19.)\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-2\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Homepage featured strip is hard-capped at 3 and the \\\"View all\\\" featured link ignores the featured filter, so the complete set of featured products cannot be browsed\", \"actual\": \"Marking works: after creating \\\"Hydrow Wave Rower\\\" with featured=on it got a \\\"Featured\\\" badge, and after unmarking Dyson in admin the homepage strip changed from [sony, peloton, dyson] to [sony, peloton, hydrow] — so marking/unmarking does update the collection. BUT with 4 products featured (sony, peloton, dyson, hydrow) the homepage strip rendered only 3 and hydrow was omitted with no way to reach it. The strip's \\\"View all\\\" link points to /products?featured=true, and that page ignores the featured query parameter entirely: it rendered \\\"10 products found\\\" listing every product including non-featured ones (macbook, theragun, philips-hue, breville, bowflex, samsung), and the heading stayed \\\"All Products\\\". There is no working view of the complete featured set.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-3\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"\\\"SONY\\\"→1 product (sony-wh-1000xm5, name match, uppercase); \\\"liquid retina\\\"→1 product (macbook-pro-14, brief-description match); \\\"FLAGSHIP\\\"→1 product (samsung-galaxy-s24-ultra, tag-only match, uppercase). Counts accurate in all cases.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-4\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Tag-filter choice list is a static hard-coded set that never reflects tags assigned to products\", \"actual\": \"Assigned the new tag \\\"qafresh\\\" (plus renamed \\\"cordless\\\"→\\\"cordless-stick\\\") to the existing product Dyson V15 Detect, and created a product with new tags \\\"rowing, qamarker, low-impact\\\". The saved tags are on the products (Dyson detail page lists qafresh; keyword search \\\"qafresh\\\" finds it). But the /products advanced tag filter still lists exactly the same 35 original tags: none of cordless-stick, qafresh, rowing, qamarker or low-impact is offered as a filter choice, so the new tag cannot be selected at all. Conversely the removed tags \\\"cleaning\\\" and \\\"cordless\\\" are still offered, and selecting \\\"cleaning\\\" yields \\\"0 products found\\\" — a dead filter option.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-5\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Created \\\"Hydrow Wave Rower\\\" with three brand-new comma-separated tag values \\\"rowing, qamarker, low-impact\\\". Its detail page renders exactly those three tags (product.tags.item.rowing / .qamarker / .low-impact). Keyword search for \\\"QAMARKER\\\" on /products returns \\\"1 product found\\\" = hydrow-wave-rower, so the new tags participate in keyword search.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-6\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Edited Dyson V15 Detect tags from \\\"vacuum, cordless, smart-home, cleaning\\\" to \\\"vacuum, cordless-stick, smart-home, qafresh\\\" — one add (qafresh), one rename (cordless→cordless-stick), one removal (cleaning). Detail page now lists exactly vacuum / cordless-stick / smart-home / qafresh. Keyword search \\\"qafresh\\\" → \\\"1 product found\\\" = dyson-v15-detect; search \\\"cleaning\\\" → \\\"0 products found\\\", confirming the removed tag no longer matches.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Admin category control is a single-select with exactly the three supported options (tech/home/fitness). Created \\\"Hydrow Wave Rower\\\" with category=Fitness; it then appeared in /category/fitness grid (4 items incl. hydrow-wave-rower) and its detail page shows exactly one category badge, \\\"Fitness\\\".\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-8\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"/products category select: Tech Gadgets → \\\"3 products found\\\" (samsung, macbook, sony, all badged Tech); Home Goods → 3 (breville, philips-hue, dyson, all Home); Fitness → 3 (bowflex, theragun, peloton, all Fitness). Grid and count update together.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-9\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"All 9 products on /products expose category badge, price, name, brief description, star rating value, image (unsplash src), and a \\\"Buy Now\\\" link to an external retailer URL.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-10\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Price-range filter is not a working range control: only one slider thumb is rendered, minimum price can never be set\", \"actual\": \"All four sorts work correctly (newest; rating 4.9→4.4; price-asc $199→$2,495; price-desc $2,495→$199) and the minimum-rating filter works (4.5+ → 8 products, all ≥4.5). However the price slider [data-semtag-id='filters.price'] contains exactly ONE [role=slider] thumb (aria-label=\\\"Minimum\\\", aria-valuenow permanently 0) although it is bound to two states (filters.price-min, filters.price-max). Dragging that single \\\"Minimum\\\" thumb changes the MAXIMUM instead (max label went $2495→$2410→$1250, count 9→8→6, correctly filtering ≤ max). The minimum price stays $0 and there is no second thumb to grab, and keyboard (ArrowRight/End) does not move the thumb at all. So visitors cannot filter by a price range, only by a maximum price.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-19\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Admin product additions/edits are in-memory only and are lost on any page reload or revisit\", \"actual\": \"Created \\\"Hydrow Wave Rower\\\" via the admin panel; it appeared immediately in the admin list (id mtc7u55jbft177545c) and the product count rose to 10. After reloading (navigating to http://localhost:7001/product/hydrow-wave-rower) the page rendered \\\"Product Not Found\\\", and /products reverted to \\\"9 products found\\\" with no Hydrow entry. localStorage and sessionStorage are both completely empty (0 keys), confirming nothing is persisted — every create/edit/delete reverts to the seeded 9 products on reload.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-11\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"All 9 seeded products carry exactly one category badge, drawn only from Tech/Home/Fitness (3 per category; 3+3+3=9 = total count). Homepage category cards also report 3 products each.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-12\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Tags apple+vacuum → 2 results (macbook has apple, dyson has vacuum) = OR within tags. Adding category=Tech narrowed to 1 (macbook only) = AND across criteria. Adding search \\\"sony\\\" on top → \\\"0 products found\\\" (no unrelated results). Price max $1250 earlier returned only the 6 products ≤ $1250; min-rating 4.5 returned only products ≥ 4.5.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-20\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Publish validation only enforces name, description and rating range; review, image, retailer link and specs are all optional, and negative prices are accepted\", \"actual\": \"Created \\\"QA Minimal Product\\\" supplying ONLY name + short description. It saved with no error, closed the form, and went live: /products now shows \\\"10 products found\\\" with a card whose <img src=\\\"\\\"> is empty and whose \\\"Buy Now\\\" href is empty (dead link). No full review and zero specifications were required. Separately, editing it to price=-50 saved successfully and the admin list renders \\\"-$50\\\"; the price input has no min attribute. The affiliate link field is type=text with no URL validation and accepted the value \\\"not-a-valid-url\\\". Only the rating field is properly constrained (min=0/max=5 blocked the value 9 with \\\"Value must be less than or equal to 5.\\\").\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-22\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"/product/nonexistent-widget-xyz → \\\"Product Not Found — The product you're looking for doesn't exist or has been removed.\\\" with a Browse All Products link, no product.name element and 0 images. /category/bogus-category → \\\"Category Not Found — The category you're looking for doesn't exist.\\\" with an empty grid. Neither leaks unrelated product data.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Typing in search (9→1), changing category, changing sort (order re-ordered), min-rating (9→8) and dragging price max (9→8→6) all updated the grid, order and the \\\"N products found\\\" count live on /products with no page reload.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Clicking the name link products.grid.item.dyson-v15-detect navigated to /product/dyson-v15-detect showing product.name \\\"Dyson V15 Detect\\\". Clicking the card IMAGE for Bowflex navigated to /product/bowflex-selecttech-552 with product.name \\\"Bowflex SelectTech 552\\\". Each card image is wrapped in an anchor to its own /product/<slug>.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Detail-page \\\"Buy Now\\\" (product.buy) has href https://example.com/dyson-v15 target=_blank rel; clicking it opened a new browser tab on that external URL. Every card/detail buy action carries its own product-specific external URL (sony-xm5, macbook-pro, s24-ultra, dyson-v15, philips-hue, breville, peloton, theragun, bowflex). Note: seed data uses example.com placeholder domains rather than a real retailer.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-21\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Category select on the category page is inert — choosing a different category changes neither the active category nor the displayed products\", \"actual\": \"On /category/fitness a category filter (filters.category) is offered with all four options (All Categories, Tech Gadgets, Home Goods, Fitness) and shows \\\"Fitness\\\". Selecting \\\"Home Goods\\\" produced no change: URL stayed /category/fitness, h1 and category.name stayed \\\"Fitness\\\", the select trigger still displayed \\\"Fitness\\\", and the grid still showed the same 3 fitness products (bowflex-selecttech-552, theragun-pro, peloton-bike-plus). Repeating with \\\"Tech Gadgets\\\" gave the identical no-op result. (The same control works correctly on /products, and the header nav category links do navigate, so the defect is specific to the category-page select.)\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Audited all 10 detail pages (9 seeded + 1 created). Each shows name, exactly one category badge, rating, formatted price, brief description, full review (408–508 chars, none clamped: scrollHeight == clientHeight), 4 tags (3 for the created one), 5 key specifications (3 for the created one), an image with a src, and a Buy Now action with a product-specific external href.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Seeded tags are topically apt and match their category: Sony=headphones/wireless/noise-cancelling/premium (Tech), MacBook=laptop/apple/professional/portable (Tech), Samsung=smartphone/android/camera/flagship (Tech), Dyson=vacuum/cordless/smart-home/cleaning (Home), Philips Hue=lighting/smart-home/ambiance/automation (Home), Breville=coffee/espresso/kitchen/appliance (Home), Peloton=cardio/cycling/smart-equipment/subscription (Fitness), Theragun=recovery/massage/muscle/therapy (Fitness), Bowflex=weights/dumbbells/strength/home-gym (Fitness). Category badge, price and rating on each detail page match the values shown on the homepage, /products grid and category grid.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Dyson V15 Detect identical across views — homepage latest-home ($749), products grid (Home, $749, 4.7, \\\"Intelligent cordless vacuum with laser dust detection and real-time particle counting.\\\"), category view, and detail page (Home, $749, 4.7, same brief description). Detail review renders in full (424 chars, computed line-clamp:none, scrollHeight 104 == clientHeight 104, no ellipsis) and all 5 specs are listed.\"}]}"
